# shell/bar — the bar's own directory (ticket 07).
#
# Two types, split by what they answer:
#
#   BarConfig  the singleton. Where the user's configuration file is, what
#              shape it has, which of its entries are usable, and the failure
#              policy for the ones that are not. It loads nothing and draws
#              nothing — it answers "what should the bar contain".
#
#   BarZone    one zone's contents, built from what BarConfig answered. It
#              resolves no names and loads no files, so configuration cannot
#              become code here either.
#
# Ticket 08 adds the bar itself here — the three zones arranged on a surface,
# the true centring, and the floating/full-width toggle.
#
# A qmldir disables Quickshell's synthetic qmldir for its directory, so every
# type here needs a line below (scripts/verify-bar-config.sh asserts this).
singleton BarConfig 1.0 BarConfig.qml
BarZone BarZone.qml